[00:01.24] (Lois Mann - Henry Bernard - Murray Burns)
[00:07.18] Well, we've been sweethearts for so long
[00:10.60] Now you say we're through
[00:13.46] The love we shared is now a memory
[00:19.04] I had built a ship of dreams
[00:23.14] And planned them all for you
[00:26.00] But now I guess what is to be will be.
[00:32.06] I gave a message to the wind to take home
[00:37.18] On to you hoping you would hear my S.O.S.
[00:44.00] I thought that you would come back home my darling
[00:49.40] Of you knew how much my aching heart was in distress.
[00:56.62] Well, I'll sail my ship alone
[01:00.16] With all the dreams I own
[01:04.08] Drifting out across the ocean blue
[01:09.74] Yes, I'll sail my ship alone
[01:13.10] Though all the sails you torn
[01:16.22] And when it starts to sink then I'll blame you.
